StructuralRule.Predicate:
FunctionCall fc: 
    fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
        f.name matches "ciphers=" 
        and f.enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
            name == "Net.HTTP"
        ]
    ]* and fc.arguments.length > 0
    and (
        /* CBC Mode */
        fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-CBC(3)?-.*"
        /* Weak Hash Functions */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-(SHA|MD5|GOST94|GOST89)"
        /* Weak Ciphers */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-(RC2|RC4|DES|3DES)-.*"
        /* Anonymous or Null algortihms */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*(ANON|NULL).*"
    )

FunctionCall fc: 
    fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
        f.name matches "ciphers=" 
        and f.enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
            name == "OpenSSL.SSL.SSLContext"
        ]
    ]* and fc.arguments.length > 0
    and (
        /* CBC Mode */
        fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-CBC(3)?-.*"
        /* Weak Hash Functions */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-(SHA|MD5|GOST94|GOST89)"
        /* Weak Ciphers */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*-(RC2|RC4|DES|3DES)-.*"
        /* Anonymous or Null algortihms */
        or fc.arguments[0].constantValue matches "(?i).*(ANON|NULL).*"
    )

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "@@?PUT_REGEX_HERE" and
            fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and fa.field is [Field f:]*
                    /*and fa.field.type.name == "String" */

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "@@?PUT_REGEX_HERE" and
            fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and fa.field is [Field f:]*
                    /*and fa.field.type.name == "String" */

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "(?i)@@?pass(wd|word)" and
            fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and fa.field is [Field f:]*
                    /*and fa.field.type.name == "String" */

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE" and
            va in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is va and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*
               /* and va.variable.type.name == "String" */

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE" and
            va in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is va and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*
               /* and va.variable.type.name == "String" */

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "(?i)pass(wd|word)" and
            va in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is va and not rhs.constantValue.null and rhs.constantValue == ""] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*
               /* and va.variable.type.name == "String" */

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "@(@)?(PUT_REGEX_HERE)"
    and fa in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === fa.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and fa.field is [Field f:]*

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "@(@)?(PUT_REGEX_HERE)"
    and fa in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === fa.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and fa.field is [Field f:]*

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "(?i)@(@)?(enc(ryption|rypt)?|crypto)(_)?key"
    and fa in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === fa.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and fa.field is [Field f:]*

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE"
    and va in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === va.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE"
    and va in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === va.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*

VariableAccess va: va.variable.name matches "(?i)((enc|dec)(ryption|rypt)?|crypto)?(_)?key|passphrase"
    and va in [AssignmentStatement:
        lhs.location is [Location l:
            l.transitiveBase === va.transitiveBase
        ] and rhs.constantValue is [Null:]
    ] and va.variable is [Variable v:]*

CharacterizationRule.Notes:
Usually setters won't have set at teh start, but just in case. Usually would use: 
attr_accessor :account

which in the background creates: 

def account()
  @account
end
def account=(var)
  @account=var
end
so need to match function ending in '=', but not those ending in '==' which are used for comparison

CharacterizationRule.StructuralMatch:
FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
    f.name matches "execute(!)?|each"
    and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
        name == "SQLite3.Statement"]
    ]
    and fc.arguments contains [Expression lambda: 
        lambda.type.name == "lambda"
        and lambda.possibleTypes contains [Type: 
            definition is [Class: 
                functions contains [Function realCall: 
                    name == "call"
                    and parameters contains [Variable p: ]
                ] 
            ]
        ] 
    ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
    f.name == "define_function"
    and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
        name == "SQLite3.Database"]
    ]
    and fc.arguments[1] is [Expression lambda: 
        lambda.type.name == "lambda"
        and lambda.possibleTypes contains [Type: 
            definition is [Class: 
                functions contains [Function realCall: 
                    name == "call"
                    and parameters contains [Variable p: ] 
                ]
            ] 
        ]
    ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
    f.name == "copy_data"
    and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
        name == "PG.Connection"]
        ]
        and fc.arguments contains [Expression lambda: 
            type.name == "lambda"
            and lambda.possibleTypes contains [Type: 
                definition is [Class: 
                    functions contains [Function: 
                        name == "call"
                        and parameters contains [Variable res: ]
                    ] 
                ]
            ]
        ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: 
    f.name matches "async_exec|async_query|exec(_params|_prepared)?|get_last_result|get_result" 
    and enclosingClass.supers contains [Class: 
        name == "PG.Connection"]
    ]
    and fc.arguments contains [Expression lambda: 
        type.name == "lambda"
        and lambda.possibleTypes contains [Type: 
            definition is [Class: 
                functions contains [Function: 
                    name == "call"
                    and parameters contains [Variable res: ]
                ] 
            ]
        ] 
    ]

FunctionCall fc: fc.possibleTargets contains [Function f: f.name matches "(self\.)?(gets|readline(s)?)" and f.enclosingClass.name == "Kernel" and f.isLibrary]
    and not fc.possibleTargets contains [Function: enclosingClass.name matches "IO|CSV|Readline"]
                /* and fc.possibleTargets.length == 1 */

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "PUT_REGEX_HERE"
    and not fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa ]
        /*and fa.field.type.name == "String"*/

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches ".*(PUT_REGEX_HERE).*"
    and not fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa ]
        /*and fa.field.type.name == "String"*/

FieldAccess fa: fa.field.name matches "(?i).*pass(wd|word|phrase).*"
    and not fa in [AssignmentStatement: lhs.location is fa ]
        /*and fa.field.type.name == "String"*/

ControlflowRule.Definition:
state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal;
state error notRequireSSL;

var c; 

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$set_ssl_mode(...) }
assignVal -> notRequireSSL { $pg_client_connect(c) | $pg_client_connect2(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_empty";
state error emptyPassword: "statedesc.ruby.empty_password_used";

var c; 

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> emptyPassword { $pg_client_connect(c) | $pg_client_connect2(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_null";
state error nilPassword: "statedesc.ruby.null_password_used";

var c; 

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> nilPassword { $pg_client_connect(c) | $pg_client_connect2(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_hardcoded";
state error hardcodePassword: "statedesc.ruby.hardcoded_password_used";

var c; 

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> hardcodePassword { $pg_client_connect(c) | $pg_client_connect2(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_empty";
state error emptyPassword: "statedesc.ruby.empty_password_used";

var c; 
var d;

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> emptyPassword { d = $mysql2_client_connect(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_null";
state error nilPassword: "statedesc.ruby.null_password_used";

var c; 
var d;

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> nilPassword { d = $mysql2_client_connect(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal: "statedesc.ruby.password_assigned_hardcoded";
state error hardcodePassword: "statedesc.ruby.hardcoded_password_used";

var c; 
var d;

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setPassword(...) }
assignVal -> hardcodePassword { d = $mysql2_client_connect(c) }

state start start;
state newHash;
state assignVal;
state error connectInsecure;

var c; 
var d;

start -> newHash { c = $hash_init(...) }
newHash -> assignVal { c.$setSecureAuth(...) }
assignVal -> connectInsecure { d = $mysql2_client_connect(c) }

state start start;
state initializeCipher: "statedesc.ruby.cipherInstantiated";
state ivChanged;
state error update: "statedesc.ruby.updateCipherOutput";

var c; 

start -> initializeCipher { c = $initCipher1(...) | c = $initCipher2(...) }
initializeCipher -> ivChanged { c.$changeIV(...) }
initializeCipher -> update { c.$update(...) }

state start start;
state initializeCipher: "statedesc.ruby.cipherInstantiated";
state update;
state error stepMissed: "statedesc.ruby.updateMissed";

var c; 

start -> initializeCipher { c = $initCipher1(...) | c = $initCipher2(...) }
initializeCipher -> update { c.$update(...) }
initializeCipher -> stepMissed { c.$padding(...) }

state start start;
state initializeCipher: "statedesc.ruby.cipherInstantiated";
state update: "statedesc.ruby.updateCipherOutput";
state pad;
state error stepMissed: "statedesc.ruby.paddingMissed";

var c; 

start -> initializeCipher { c = $initCipher1(...) | c = $initCipher2(...) }
initializeCipher -> update { c.$update(...) }

update -> pad { c.$padding(...) }
update -> stepMissed { #end_scope(c) }

state start start;
state initializeCipher: "statedesc.ruby.cipherInstantiated";
state safe: "statedesc.ruby.cipherModeInit";
state error stepMissed: "statedesc.ruby.encryptionModeMissed";

var c; 

start -> initializeCipher { c = $initCipher1(...) | c = $initCipher2(...) }
initializeCipher -> safe { c.$safe(...) }
initializeCipher -> stepMissed { c.$runMethod(...) }

state start start;
state createContext;
state setSSLVersion;
state error sslVersionNotSet: "statedesc.ruby.weakSSLProtocol";

var c;

start -> createContext { c = $initContext(...) }
createContext -> setSSLVersion { c.$setSSLVersion(...) }
createContext -> sslVersionNotSet { $useContext(..., c) }

Description.Explanation:
XML Entity Expansion injection also known as XML Bombs are DoS attacks that benefit from valid and well-formed XML blocks that expand exponentially until they exhaust the server allocated resources. XML allows to define custom entities which act as string substitution macros. By nesting recurrent entity resolutions, an attacker may easily crash the server resources.

The following XML document shows an example of an XML Bomb.
<pre>
&lt;?xml version="1.0"?&gt;
&lt;!DOCTYPE lolz [
  &lt;!ENTITY lol "lol"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol2 "&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;&amp;lol;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol3 "&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;&amp;lol2;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol4 "&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;&amp;lol3;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol5 "&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;&amp;lol4;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol6 "&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;&amp;lol5;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol7 "&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;&amp;lol6;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol8 "&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;&amp;lol7;"&gt;
  &lt;!ENTITY lol9 "&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;&amp;lol8;"&gt;
]&gt;
&lt;lolz&gt;&amp;lol9;&lt;/lolz&gt;
</pre>

This test could crash the server by expanding the small XML document into more than 3GB in memory.
